 are B suit and some T suit in hand \u2192 not one suit. All Types needs all 3 suits + winds + dragons: currently I have W, T, B, and wind (F3). No dragon yet. Could aim for it, but long shot.  \n\nGiven opponents' melds:  \n- Across player has two W chows and one T chow, so W and T tiles are being used.  \n- Next player has B1-B3 chow.  \n\nBest discard is likely **B6** or **B7** because they are already used in a meld, so they are deadwood in hand.  \n\nChoosing **B6**:  \n- B6 unshown: 2 left, B7 unshown: 2 left. Both similar.  \n- Keeping T4,T5,T6,T7 gives best chance for T chows.  \n- Keeping F3 may give 1 fan if I pung it later.  \n- Keeping W3 maybe for a pair if W3 appears again (only 1 left), unlikely.  \n\nDiscard **B6** seems safe and keeps flexibility.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nDiscarding B6 removes a tile that's already part of an exposed meld, so it's useless in hand. Keeping T tiles maintains potential for T chows, and keeping F3 keeps possible honor pung for small fan. Hand after discard: W3, T4, T5, T6, T7, B7, F3 \u2192 still need two more melds + pair, but now no redundant B tiles.  \n\n**Answer:** Play B6"}
